<h1>Hardware Settings - Scan Mode Tab</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description: Scan Mode</b></span> Tab allows the change of settings related to the scanning procedure.</p>
<p><img src="../images/hw_scanning.gif" width="551px" height="485px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The tab is divided in three sections and five single options to check:</span></p>
<p class="sub-head">Auto save during pause</p>
<p>The options in this group are Off by default. To enable it, the user should check one of the check-boxes and select name and path for saving the file.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>File prefix</b></span> edit box:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Type a name or leave the default one (KubeSave_01.sab2 and KubeSave_02.sab2 for the scan session backup files and KubeSave_<span style="font-style:italic;"><i>N</i></span>.sab2 for the patch backup files, where <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>N</i></span> is the subsequent number of every patch captured, starting from 0).</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Path</b></span> edit box:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Type the path or use "Browse" button to select the folder, where the scan file(s) will be saved. The default path is located in current user's Temp folder.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Create file for scan session</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Choose this option to save all scanned patches in a single file. The save process will be run during scan pause.</p>
<p class="Warning">When this option is enabled, a backup copy of the previous file is created every time a patch is created (after the second patch). If we assume that KubeSave is the file prefix this means that after the first patch the result is <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>KubeSave_01.sab2</i></span>. After the second patch the result is <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>KubeSave_02.sab2</i></span> (with two patches) and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>KubeSave_01.sab2</i></span> is the backup copy (with one patch). After the third patch the result is <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>KubeSave_01.sab2</i></span> (with three patches) and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>KubeSave_02.sab2</i></span> is the backup copy (with two patches) and so on. A hint for distinguishing the result (last created file) from the backup copy is the file size - the result is always with larger file size.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Create file per patch</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Choose this option to save each scanned patch in a separate file. Each file will have the given name and a number, corresponding to the patch scanning order.</p>
<p>If both options are checked, then each scanned patch will be saved in a separate file and all the patches will also be saved in the common file during the pause.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><span><span style="text-decoration:none;">I</span></span>mmediate View during pause</p>
<p>This group is not enabled by default. If activated (using the group checkbox) it allows quick switching between view and scanning modes. The user can choose one of the following modes:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Press and hold mode</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">It is the default option. If enabled, the user can enter the view mode straight from the pause mode by pressing and holding on the "B" button (right remote control button or pedal switch). Adjust the best view position and when ready release the "B" button. You will be automatically back to the pause mode.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Press and release mode</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If enabled, the user can enter the view mode straight from the pause mode by pressing on the "B" button (right remote control button or pedal switch) and releasing it after 2-3 seconds. The view mode will be activated. Adjust the best view position and when ready press and release again the button after 2-3 seconds. You will be automatically back to the pause mode.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Rendering while capture data Group</p>
<p>Enables the user to select the way captured data is displayed while scanning. Two options are available: <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>points</b></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>shaded</b></span>. Points is the default option.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Rendering during pause Group</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Normal line</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets the guiding stripe thickness and colour to the default values - one pixel width and white colour (on black background).</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Wider line</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets custom width and colour for the guiding stripe:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>... pts</b></span> field - width of the guiding stripe in pixels.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Colour</b></span> listbox - colour of the guiding stripe.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> Colours in the list are valid for black background only. For other backgrounds colours may vary.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" id="p1">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Scan options for:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Activate fast scanning via trigger button</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This option is used with ModelMaker D sensors only. When the checkbox is enabled KUBE can switch to from normal scan mode to fast scan mode and vice versa by double-clicking the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' (trigger) button. Otherwise this functionality is disabled. The option is enabled by default. For details about scanning rates, see <a href="Hardware_Settings_-_Sensor_Tab_MMD.htm#Turbo">Turbo functionality</a> in advanced settings.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Remove last patch</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This option allows the user to remove the last scanned patch when necessary. In pause mode press on the "A" button (left remote control button or pedal switch) and release it after 2-3 seconds. A message will appear asking you whether to delete the last scanned patch or not. Confirm it to return to pause mode.</p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: This option works one step back only. If you activate <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Remove last patch</b></span> again and the last patch has been already removed, an appropriate warning will appear, then you will return to the pause mode.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Enter scan mode immediately after prescan/autoset mode</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>T</b></span>his option allows the user to begin scanning right after performing the prescan or autoset (in this case scan mode is entered only if there are some data loaded / scanned). Enabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Check system speed while scanning</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This option allows the user to check the system speed while scanning to ensure good quality of the scan data. Enabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Limit captured points to</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This option allows the user to limit the scanned points in the current document. If it is enabled, a warning message will appear when the input number of scan points is reached. The user can choose continue or cancel the scanning process. The option is disabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use standoff indicator bar</b></span> button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Enables and disables the standoff indicator bar at the bottom of the KUBE application window. Click on the button to:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">enable it: <img src="../images/stand_off.gif" width="210px" height="12px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">disable it: &#160;<img src="../images/stand_off_off.gif" width="210px" height="12px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</li>
</ul>

